WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — rce-compile (30s) Narrator Lem

1
00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.456
Developers pass dash-O-three by reflex,

2
00:00:02.456 --> 00:00:06.905
assuming faster binaries always pay back the heavy energy spent compiling them.

3
00:00:07.026 --> 00:00:09.216
Audited across twelve compiler families,

4
00:00:09.216 --> 00:00:13.869
a universal statement failed as description and survived as a seven-part normal form.

5
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.010
Across 20 kernels and 14 compiler tiers on Zen 5 RAPL,

6
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:24.487
jumping from O0 to O3 needs over 50,000 runs—and 30 percent of O3 jumps never pay back.

7
00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:29.181
Indexing binaries by De Bruijn nameless hashes hits zero

8
00:00:29.181 --> 00:00:34.000
false collisions and cuts warm rustc O3 energy 448.5 times.
